<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Solder</displayName>
  <description>Settings for Solder, the coding agent in VS Code, enforced by your organization.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_Solder">Solder 0.2.5 or later, in VS Code on Windows (Tool models and Assist session block: 0.2.8 or later; skills and feedback address: 0.2.9 or later; Assist models: 0.2.10 or later)</string>
      <string id="Cat_Solder">Solder</string>
      <string id="Cat_Connection">Connection</string>
      <string id="Cat_Model">Model</string>
      <string id="Cat_Docs">Docs</string>
      <string id="Cat_Skills">Skills</string>
      <string id="Cat_Support">Support</string>
      <string id="Cat_Rules">Rules and instructions</string>
      <string id="Cat_Limits">Limits</string>

      <string id="Endpoint">Gateway address</string>
      <string id="Endpoint_Help">The full Chat Completions URL Solder connects to, ending in /chat/completions, for example https://gateway.example.com/v1/chat/completions.

Enabled: Solder uses this address and users can't change it. If it isn't a valid address, Solder won't connect (it doesn't fall back to the user's own).
Not configured: users set their own.

Each user still sets their own API key: keys are never set by policy.</string>
      <string id="Model">Default model</string>
      <string id="Model_Help">The model id Solder uses. Enabled: users can't pick another model, for new chats or existing ones.</string>
      <string id="ModelFilter">Models offered</string>
      <string id="ModelFilter_Help">A regular expression: only models whose id matches are offered in the model picker, for example -tools$ or ^(model-a|model-b)$.</string>
      <string id="AssistModels">Assist models</string>
      <string id="AssistModels_Help">The Assist models, by id, one per line: plain-text models Solder reaches through its written protocol (and the gateway's sessions). Every other model is a Tool model (a system prompt and native tool calls). This is what users set in Settings → Advanced → Kinds of model.

Enabled: these are the Assist models, and users can't change which models are which. Not configured: users choose, or "Tool models" (a pattern) decides.</string>
      <string id="ToolModels">Tool models</string>
      <string id="ToolModels_Help">A regular expression: models whose id matches are Tool models (a system prompt and native tool calls). Every other model is an Assist model, which takes plain text only and is reached through Solder's text protocol and the gateway's sessions. Not configured or empty: every model is a Tool model.</string>
      <string id="AssistSessionBlock">Assist session block</string>
      <string id="AssistSessionBlock_Help">The name of the object in the gateway's responses that carries an Assist model's session. Not configured or empty: no sessions, so every Assist request carries the conversation over in one message.</string>
      <string id="ModelNames">Model display names</string>
      <string id="ModelNames_Help">Short names for model ids in the picker, as JSON, for example {"model-a": "Model A"}.</string>
      <string id="Effort">Effort</string>
      <string id="Effort_Help">How hard the model thinks. Default sends nothing (the model's own choice). Enabled: users can't change it, in settings or per chat.</string>
      <string id="Effort_Default">Default (the model's own choice)</string>
      <string id="Effort_Low">Low</string>
      <string id="Effort_Medium">Medium</string>
      <string id="Effort_High">High (slower, many more tokens)</string>

      <string id="DocsFolders">Docs folders</string>
      <string id="DocsFolders_Help">Folders of reference docs Solder searches, one per line. A short note on what's in a folder can follow a | character, for example:
\\fileserver\docs\api|The in-house API reference
C:\Specs

Enabled: these folders are searched. Users can't change them, or add their own unless "Let users add docs folders" is also enabled.</string>
      <string id="AllowUserDocsFolders">Let users add docs folders</string>
      <string id="AllowUserDocsFolders_Help">With "Docs folders" enforced: Enabled lets users add folders of their own beside the organization's (which they still can't remove). Disabled or not configured: only the organization's folders.</string>
      <string id="SkillsFolders">Skills folders</string>
      <string id="SkillsFolders_Help">Folders of skills, one per line, for example:
\\fileserver\it\solder-skills

A skill is instructions for a kind of task: one .md file directly in a folder, named after the skill (code_review.md), whose first line says when to use it ("When to use: Reviewing a change before it's committed."). The model is told each skill's name and when to use it, and reads one whole before a task it covers.

Enabled: these folders' skills are offered to every user. Users see them in Settings but can't remove the folders, or add their own unless "Let users add skills folders" is also enabled. Solder reads the folders; users only need read access.</string>
      <string id="AllowUserSkills">Let users add skills folders</string>
      <string id="AllowUserSkills_Help">With "Skills folders" enforced: Enabled lets users add skills folders of their own beside the organization's (which they still can't remove), and save new skills there. Disabled or not configured: only the organization's skills.</string>
      <string id="DocsSearch">Docs search</string>
      <string id="DocsSearch_Help">Keywords: the docs index stays on the PC, and only the passages the model reads are sent to the gateway. Keywords and meaning: every passage is also sent to the gateway once, to its embeddings model. Enforce Keywords to keep docs text from being sent for embedding.</string>
      <string id="DocsSearch_Keyword">Keywords</string>
      <string id="DocsSearch_Hybrid">Keywords and meaning</string>
      <string id="EmbeddingModel">Embeddings model</string>
      <string id="EmbeddingModel_Help">The gateway's embeddings model id, for search by meaning.</string>

      <string id="Rules">Rules (replace the user's)</string>
      <string id="Rules_Help">The rules the model follows, one per line, in place of the user's own. Users can't change them. To add organization rules while keeping the user's, use "Organization rules" instead.</string>
      <string id="OrgRules">Organization rules</string>
      <string id="OrgRules_Help">Rules every user's chats follow, one per line. They're added after the user's own rules, so they read as the more recent instruction; users see them in Settings but can't change them.</string>
      <string id="InstructionFiles">Instruction files</string>
      <string id="InstructionFiles_Help">File names in the workspace the model follows, one per line, for example AGENTS.md. Plain names only.</string>

      <string id="CompactAtTokens">Compact at tokens</string>
      <string id="CompactAtTokens_Help">When the older part of a chat is summarized to save tokens (30,000 or more).</string>
      <string id="MaxRounds">Max rounds</string>
      <string id="MaxRounds_Help">The most steps with tool calls for one message (1 to 100).</string>
      <string id="StorageLimitGB">Storage limit (GB)</string>
      <string id="StorageLimitGB_Help">The most disk space Undo's backups may use; past it, the oldest go first.</string>

      <string id="FeedbackAddress">Feedback address</string>
      <string id="FeedbackAddress_Help">The email address Solder's Send feedback goes to, for example solder-feedback@example.com, instead of Solder's own support address (support@gremnar.com). Use it to keep feedback, which may mention your code or projects, inside your organization.

Send feedback only opens the user's own email app with the address filled in; Solder itself sends nothing.

Enabled: feedback goes to this address. If it isn't a usable email address, Send feedback says so and opens nothing: it never falls back to Solder's own address. The same happens while your policy can't be read.
Not configured: feedback goes to Solder's support address.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="Endpoint"><textBox refId="Endpoint"><label>Gateway address:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="Model"><textBox refId="Model"><label>Model id:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="ModelFilter"><textBox refId="ModelFilter"><label>Regular expression:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="AssistModels"><multiTextBox refId="AssistModels">Model ids, one per line:</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="ToolModels"><textBox refId="ToolModels"><label>Regular expression:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="AssistSessionBlock"><textBox refId="AssistSessionBlock"><label>Block name:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="ModelNames"><textBox refId="ModelNames"><label>JSON:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="Effort"><dropdownList refId="Effort" noSort="true" defaultItem="0">Effort:</dropdownList></presentation>
      <presentation id="DocsFolders"><multiTextBox refId="DocsFolders">Folders, one per line (path|note):</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="FeedbackAddress"><textBox refId="FeedbackAddress"><label>Email address:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="SkillsFolders"><multiTextBox refId="SkillsFolders">Folders, one per line:</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="DocsSearch"><dropdownList refId="DocsSearch" noSort="true" defaultItem="0">Search by:</dropdownList></presentation>
      <presentation id="EmbeddingModel"><textBox refId="EmbeddingModel"><label>Model id:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="Rules"><multiTextBox refId="Rules">Rules, one per line:</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="OrgRules"><multiTextBox refId="OrgRules">Rules, one per line:</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="InstructionFiles"><multiTextBox refId="InstructionFiles">File names, one per line:</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="CompactAtTokens"><decimalTextBox refId="CompactAtTokens" defaultValue="100000">Tokens:</decimalTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="MaxRounds"><decimalTextBox refId="MaxRounds" defaultValue="30">Rounds:</decimalTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="StorageLimitGB"><decimalTextBox refId="StorageLimitGB" defaultValue="5">GB:</decimalTextBox></presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
